Package: lucid-dock
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: lucid-session
Description: magnifying macOS-style dock for Wayland
 A dock for Wayland compositors that implement wlr-layer-shell, implemented as
 an ordinary layer-shell client rather than as part of a compositor. A dock that
 crashes should cost you a dock, not your session.
 .
 Icons magnify under the pointer with a damped spring derived from the reference
 implementation rather than tuned by eye, applications that are running are
 marked using the foreign-toplevel protocols rather than by guessing at process
 names, and the panel's geometry, motion and stylesheet values are settings with
 provenance rather than constants.
 .
 This package is useful on its own: it works on KWin, sway, Hyprland, labwc and
 COSMIC, and does not require the rest of LucidOS. It does not work on GNOME,
 because Mutter does not implement wlr-layer-shell.
